# text = On the death of his father , Ralph Nickleby , who had been some time before placed in a mercantile house in London , applied himself passionately to his old pursuit of money-getting , in which he speedily became so buried and absorbed , that he quite forgot his brother for many years ; and if , at times , a recollection of his old playfellow broke upon him through the haze in which he lived -- for gold conjures up a mist about a man , more destructive of all his old senses and lulling to his feelings than the fumes of charcoal -- it brought along with it a companion thought , that if they were intimate he would want to borrow money of him .
