# text = In a corner of the seat , was a very small deal trunk , tied round with a scanty piece of cord ; and on the trunk was perched -- his lace-up half-boots and corduroy trousers dangling in the air -- a diminutive boy , with his shoulders drawn up to his ears , and his hands planted on his knees , who glanced timidly at the schoolmaster , from time to time , with evident dread and apprehension muttered Mr Squeers , turning from the window , and looking sulkily at the coffee-room clock Much vexed by this reflection , Mr Squeers looked at the little boy to see whether he was doing anything he could beat him for .
