# text = Nicholas bowed , said he was very well , and seemed very much astonished at the outward appearance of the proprietor of Dotheboys Hall : as indeed he was said Ralph , looking narrowly at the schoolmaster replied Squeers rejoined Ralph said Ralph , finishing the sentence rejoined Squeers Ralph smiled , as if he meant anything but smiling , and looked round at the strangers present said Wackford Squeers , pointing to the little boy on the trunk and the two little boys on the floor , who had been staring at each other without uttering a word , and writhing their bodies into most remarkable contortions , according to the custom of little boys when they first become acquainted interrupted Ralph , testily replied Squeers interrupted Mr Snawley interrupted Ralph , checking the torrent of recommendation rejoined Squeers repeated Master Belling said Ralph said Squeers repeated Master Belling said Squeers repeated Master Belling again said Squeers suggested Nicholas , good-naturedly said Master Belling said Squeers , darting a withering look at the culprit said Ralph said Squeers resumed Ralph said Squeers answered Squeers said Ralph said Squeers , perplexed with such an application from a youth of Nicholas's figure said Ralph said Nicholas , addressing Mr Squeers replied Squeers , looking as grave as he could , and considerably puzzled , no less by the contrast between the simplicity of the nephew and the worldly manner of the uncle , than by the incomprehensible allusion to the young noblemen under his tuition said Ralph rejoined Squeers said Ralph observed the schoolmaster said Mr Snawley , thinking it as well to back his new friend occasionally said Ralph replied Squeers , half imitating the sneer with which the old gentleman was regarding his unconscious relative said Nicholas , eagerly said Ralph , in the same dry , hard manner said Squeers , answering a nod of Ralph's head with a nod of his own rejoined Ralph
