# text = After a murmur of approbation from the other passengers , during which the fastidious lady drank a glass of punch unobserved , the grey-headed gentleman thus went on said the merry-faced gentleman , emptying his glass returned the other , courteously , but in a grave and sad tone of voice said the gentleman with the merry face said the other , gently said the first speaker , with much feeling said the gentleman who had told the story retorted the other interposed the other said the grey-haired gentleman after a short reflection replied the other After a very brief silence , the merry-faced gentleman sent round the punch , and glancing slyly at the fastidious lady , who seemed desperately apprehensive that he was going to relate something improper , began THE BARON OF GROGZWIG ' The Baron Von Koeldwethout , of Grogzwig in Germany , was as likely a young baron as you would wish to see .
