# text = Upon every one of these anniversaries , the venerable Baroness Von Swillenhausen was nervously sensitive for the well-being of her child the Baroness Von Koeldwethout ; and although it was not found that the good lady ever did anything material towards contributing to her child's recovery , still she made it a point of duty to be as nervous as possible at the castle of Grogzwig , and to divide her time between moral observations on the baron's housekeeping , and bewailing the hard lot of her unhappy daughter .
