# text = There were little faces which should have been handsome , darkened with the scowl of sullen , dogged suffering ; there was childhood with the light of its eye quenched , its beauty gone , and its helplessness alone remaining ; there were vicious-faced boys , brooding , with leaden eyes , like malefactors in a jail ; and there were young creatures on whom the sins of their frail parents had descended , weeping even for the mercenary nurses they had known , and lonesome even in their loneliness .
