# text = Miss Squeers and the miller's daughter , being fast friends , had covenanted together some two years before , according to a custom prevalent among young ladies , that whoever was first engaged to be married , should straightway confide the mighty secret to the bosom of the other , before communicating it to any living soul , and bespeak her as bridesmaid without loss of time ; in fulfilment of which pledge the miller's daughter , when her engagement was formed , came out express , at eleven o'clock at night as the corn-factor's son made an offer of his hand and heart at twenty-five minutes past ten by the Dutch clock in the kitchen , and rushed into Miss Squeers's bedroom with the gratifying intelligence .
