# text = On the second morning after the departure of Nicholas for Yorkshire , Kate Nickleby sat in a very faded chair raised upon a very dusty throne in Miss La Creevy's room , giving that lady a sitting for the portrait upon which she was engaged ; and towards the full perfection of which , Miss La Creevy had had the street-door case brought upstairs , in order that she might be the better able to infuse into the counterfeit countenance of Miss Nickleby , a bright salmon flesh - tint which she had originally hit upon while executing the miniature of a young officer therein contained , and which bright salmon flesh - tint was considered , by Miss La Creevy's chief friends and patrons , to be quite a novelty in art : as indeed it was said Miss La Creevy replied Kate , smiling rejoined Miss La Creevy observed Kate said Miss La Creevy said Kate , humouring her good - natured little friend replied Miss La Creevy said Kate answered Miss La Creevy said Kate , laughing replied Miss La Creevy said Miss La Creevy , sinking her voice to a confidential whisper Kate seemed highly amused by this information , and Miss La Creevy went on painting and talking , with immovable complacency said Kate , availing herself of a pause in the discourse , and glancing round the room inquired Miss La Creevy , looking up from her work said Miss La Creevy Drawing herself up , as though she plumed herself greatly upon not resorting to these lures to catch sitters , Miss La Creevy applied herself , more intently , to her task : only raising her head occasionally , to look with unspeakable satisfaction at some touch she had just put in : and now and then giving Miss Nickleby to understand what particular feature she was at work upon , at the moment she expressly observed said Miss La Creevy , after a long silence , to wit , an interval of full a minute and a half replied Kate inquired Miss La Creevy rejoined Kate remarked Miss La Creevy , who was an odd little mixture of shrewdness and simplicity said Kate cried Miss La Creevy observed Kate , timidly observed the miniature painter said Kate , with energy cried Miss La Creevy said Kate exclaimed Miss La Creevy replied Kate , speaking more gently Miss La Creevy looked slyly at her companion , as if she doubted whether Ralph himself were not the subject of dislike , but seeing that her young friend was distressed , made no remark continued Kate , whose tears fell while she spoke
