# text = Miss La Creevy , who was a member of the little council , ventured to insinuate some doubts relative to the probability of Miss Nickleby's arriving at this happy consummation in the compass of an ordinary lifetime ; but the good lady set that question entirely at rest , by informing them that she had a presentiment on the subject -- a species of second-sight with which she had been in the habit of clenching every argument with the deceased Mr Nickleby , and , in nine cases and three-quarters out of every ten , determining it the wrong way said Miss La Creevy observed Mrs Nickleby suggested Miss La Creevy returned Mrs Nickleby
