# text = There was , of course , a profound silence , during which Nicholas showed his disgust as plainly as looks could show it said Squeers , eyeing him maliciously replied Nicholas , in a quiet manner sneered Squeers sneered Squeers replied Nicholas said Squeers in a taunting fashion replied Nicholas Mrs Squeers had listened to this conversation , from the bottom of the stairs ; but , now losing all patience , she hastily assumed her night-jacket , and made her way to the scene of action said the lady , as the boys fell off right and left , to save her the trouble of clearing a passage with her brawny arms said Squeers said the lady said Nicholas said the excited lady replied Nicholas said Mrs Squeers , mimicking , as nearly as she could , the voice and manner of the usher said Squeers retorted Mrs Squeers , contemptuously With these words , Mrs Squeers dismissed the boys , and after a little light skirmishing with those in the rear who were pressing forward to get out of the way , but were detained for a few moments by the throng in front , succeeded in clearing the room , when she confronted her spouse alone said Mrs Squeers inquired Squeers said Mrs Squeers angrily replied Squeers rejoined Mrs Squeers laughed Squeers said Mrs S exclaimed Squeers , clapping his hands replied his wife
