# text = Nicholas hardly dared to look out of the window ; but he did so , and the very first object that met his eyes was the wretched Smike : so bedabbled with mud and rain , so haggard and worn , and wild , that , but for his garments being such as no scarecrow was ever seen to wear , he might have been doubtful , even then , of his identity said Squeers , after he had literally feasted his eyes , in silence , upon the culprit cried Mrs Squeers , as her husband proffered his assistance With hands trembling with delight , Squeers unloosened the cord ; and Smike , to all appearance more dead than alive , was brought into the house and securely locked up in a cellar , until such time as Mr Squeers should deem it expedient to operate upon him , in presence of the assembled school .
