# text = In truth , there appeared some reason to expect that such a result would follow from the encounter , for John Browdie no sooner saw Nicholas advancing , than he reined in his horse by the footpath , and waited until such time as he should come up ; looking meanwhile , very sternly between the horse's ears , at Nicholas , as he came on at his leisure said John said Nicholas observed John , making the stirrup ring under a smart touch of the ash stick replied Nicholas , hesitating he said , frankly , after a moment's pause cried the good-humoured Yorkshireman at the same time , he bent down from the saddle , and gave Nicholas's fist a huge wrench said Nicholas , turning scarlet as he spoke exclaimed John Browdie . ' Well deane !
