# text = I loike said Nicholas , not very well knowing how to make the avowal interposed John Browdie , in a tone of compassion ; for he was a giant in strength and stature , and Nicholas , very likely , in his eyes , seemed a mere dwarf replied Nicholas cried John Browdie , with such an ecstatic shout , that the horse quite shied at it With these expressions of delight , John Browdie laughed and laughed again -- so loud that the echoes , far and wide , sent back nothing but jovial peals of merriment -- and shook Nicholas by the hand meanwhile , no less heartily .
