# text = Newman Noggs accordingly read as follows A profound silence succeeded to the reading of this choice epistle , during which Newman Noggs , as he folded it up , gazed with a kind of grotesque pity at the boy of desperate character therein referred to ; who , having no more distinct perception of the matter in hand , than that he had been the unfortunate cause of heaping trouble and falsehood upon Nicholas , sat mute and dispirited , with a most woe-begone and heart-stricken look said Nicholas , after a few moments' reflection cried Newman said Nicholas said Newman rejoined Nicholas firmly , as he prepared to leave the house said Newman , planting himself before his impetuous young friend asked Nicholas , chafing violently , and pacing the narrow room with rapid strides rejoined Newman demanded Nicholas , precipitately said Newman , speaking for the moment , in his earnestness , like any other man replied Nicholas , after some consideration Newman , who had stood during the foregoing conversation with his back planted against the door , ready to oppose any egress from the apartment by force , if necessary , resumed his seat with much satisfaction ; and as the water in the kettle was by this time boiling , made a glassful of spirits and water for Nicholas , and a cracked mug-full for the joint accommodation of himself and Smike , of which the two partook in great harmony , while Nicholas , leaning his head upon his hand , remained buried in melancholy meditation .
