# text = Kate might have said , that mourning is sometimes the coldest wear which mortals can assume ; that it not only chills the breasts of those it clothes , but extending its influence to summer friends , freezes up their sources of good-will and kindness , and withering all the buds of promise they once so liberally put forth , leaves nothing but bared and rotten hearts exposed .
