# text = The life to which poor Kate Nickleby was devoted , in consequence of the unforeseen train of circumstances already developed in this narrative , was a hard one ; but lest the very dulness , unhealthy confinement , and bodily fatigue , which made up its sum and substance , should deprive it of any interest with the mass of the charitable and sympathetic , I would rather keep Miss Nickleby herself in view just now , than chill them in the outset , by a minute and lengthened description of the establishment presided over by Madame Mantalini said Miss Knag , as Kate was taking her weary way homewards on the first night of her novitiate said Madame Mantalini in reply said Miss Knag inquired Madame replied Miss Knag , reddening suggested Madame rejoined Miss Knag most complacently observed Madame Mantalini , glancing with affected carelessness at her assistant , and laughing heartily in her sleeve said Miss Knag remarked Madame Mantalini cried Miss Knag with a countenance beaming delight In fact , Miss Knag had conceived an incipient affection for Kate Nickleby , after witnessing her failure that morning , and this short conversation with her superior increased the favourable prepossession to a most surprising extent ; which was the more remarkable , as when she first scanned that young lady's face and figure , she had entertained certain inward misgivings that they would never agree said Miss Knag , glancing at the reflection of herself in a mirror at no great distance
