# text = At intervals were heard the tread of slipshod feet , and the chilly cry of the poor sweep as he crept , shivering , to his early toil ; the heavy footfall of the official watcher of the night , pacing slowly up and down and cursing the tardy hours that still intervened between him and sleep ; the rambling of ponderous carts and waggons ; the roll of the lighter vehicles which carried buyers and sellers to the different markets ; the sound of ineffectual knocking at the doors of heavy sleepers -- all these noises fell upon the ear from time to time , but all seemed muffled by the fog , and to be rendered almost as indistinct to the ear as was every object to the sight .
# sent_id = 1231
