# text = Hills swelling above each other ; and undulations shapely and uncouth , smooth and rugged , graceful and grotesque , thrown negligently side by side , bounded the view in each direction ; while frequently , with unexpected noise , there uprose from the ground a flight of crows , who , cawing and wheeling round the nearest hills , as if uncertain of their course , suddenly poised themselves upon the wing and skimmed down the long vista of some opening valley , with the speed of light itself .
