# text = The gentlemen entreated him not to hurry himself ; and , to beguile the interval , had a fencing bout with their walking-sticks on the very small landing-place : to the unspeakable discomposure of all the other lodgers downstairs said Nicholas , when he had completed his toilet said Mr Lenville , stepping into the front room , and taking his hat off , before he could get in at all said Nicholas returned Mr Lenville said Nicholas asked Mr Lenville , poking the struggling fire with his walking-stick , and afterwards wiping it on the skirt of his coat said Nicholas exclaimed Mr Lenville said Nicholas cried Mr Lenville said Nicholas said Mr Lenville inquired Mr Folair , anxiously said Nicholas sighed Mr Folair replied Nicholas said Mr Folair said Mr Lenville , observing the disturbed looks of the young dramatist rejoined Nicholas reasoned Mr Lenville replied Mr Folair Profiting by these and other lessons , which were the result of the personal experience of the two actors , Nicholas willingly gave them the best breakfast he could , and , when he at length got rid of them , applied himself to his task : by no means displeased to find that it was so much easier than he had at first supposed .
