# text = Now , Mrs Curdle was supposed , by those who were best informed on such points , to possess quite the London taste in matters relating to literature and the drama ; and as to Mr Curdle , he had written a pamphlet of sixty-four pages , post octavo , on the character of the Nurse's deceased husband in Romeo and Juliet , with an inquiry whether he really had been a ' merry man ' in his lifetime , or whether it was merely his widow's affectionate partiality that induced her so to report him .
