# text = Regardless of this circumstance , however , Mrs Lillyvick refused to be comforted until the belligerents had passed their words that the dispute should be carried no further , which , after a sufficient show of reluctance , they did , and from that time Mr Folair sat in moody silence , contenting himself with pinching Nicholas's leg when anything was said , and so expressing his contempt both for the speaker and the sentiments to which he gave utterance .
