# text = ' Upon my soul , it's a most delightful thing ," said Lord Frederick , pressing forward Mrs Nickleby was too much flurried by these uncommonly kind salutations , and her regrets at not having on her other bonnet , to make any immediate reply , so she merely continued to bend and smile , and betray great agitation said Lord Frederick returned Mrs Nickleby , recovering said Mrs Nickleby reflecting Having pretty well run herself out by this time , Mrs Nickleby stopped as suddenly as she had started off ; and repeated that Kate was quite well said Mrs Nickleby growled Ralph , pointing to the little packet Mrs Nickleby held in her hand replied Mrs Nickleby cried Sir Mulberry , seizing upon the chance of discovering where Mrs Nickleby had come from said Mrs Nickleby urged Sir Mulberry said Mrs Nickleby remarked Lord Frederick , with a solemn aspect said Mrs Nickleby replied Sir Mulberry rejoined Mrs Nickleby replied Ralph impatiently returned Mrs Nickleby said Ralph , who seldom offered refreshments unless something was to be got by it returned Mrs Nickleby , glancing at the dial said Sir Mulberry said Mrs Nickleby .
