# text = Mrs Nickleby curtseyed and smiled , and curtseyed again , and remarked , rubbing her hands as she did so , that she hadn't the -- really -- the honour to said the first gentleman answered the other gentleman said the first gentleman answered the second said the first gentleman said Pyke , reproachfully said Mr Pluck , looking round Mr Pyke laid his hand upon his heart , and bowed low said Mr Pluck observed Mrs Nickleby , graciously said Mr Pluck , drawing a chair close to Mrs Nickleby , and sitting himself down said Mrs Nickleby , and the poor lady exulted in the idea that she was marvellously sly exclaimed Mr Pluck echoed Pyke repeated Pluck replied Pyke said Mr Pluck said his friend muttered Mr Pluck , after a short pause thought Mrs Nickleby within herself Mr Pluck , after feigning to be in a condition of great embarrassment for some minutes , resumed the conversation by entreating Mrs Nickleby to take no heed of what he had inadvertently said -- to consider him imprudent , rash , injudicious .
