# text = The only stipulation he would make in his own favour was , that she should give him credit for the best intentions said Mr Pluck said Pyke replied Mrs Nickleby said Mrs Nickleby said Mr Pyke exclaimed Mr Pluck cried Mr Pyke replied Mr Pluck said Pyke , as if suddenly recollecting himself exclaimed that good lady , to whose mind a definite proposal of marriage for Kate at once presented itself in lively colours replied Pyke said Mrs Nickleby said Mr Pluck said Mrs Nickleby retorted Mr Pluck said Pyke urged Pluck said Mrs Nickleby , hesitating remonstrated Mr Pluck replied the worthy lady urged Mr Pluck said that excellent gentleman , lowering his voice Mrs Nickleby cast an apprehensive glance at the warlike Pyke , who had walked to the window ; and Mr Pluck , squeezing her hand , went on cried Mr Pyke at this juncture , snatching something from the chimney-piece with a theatrical air asked Mr Pluck cried Mr Pyke , falling into his chair with a miniature in his hand exclaimed Mr Pluck in a fit of enthusiasm said Mrs Nickleby , with great pride .
