# text = Above all things she commended a strict maidenly reserve , as being not only a very laudable thing in itself , but as tending materially to strengthen and increase a lover's ardour added Mrs Nickleby With which sentiment , and various hints of the pleasure she derived from the knowledge that her daughter inherited so large an instalment of her own excellent sense and discretion ( to nearly the full measure of which she might hope , with care , to succeed in time ), Mrs Nickleby concluded a very long and rather illegible letter .
