# text = Poor Kate was well-nigh distracted on the receipt of four closely - written and closely-crossed sides of congratulation on the very subject which had prevented her closing her eyes all night , and kept her weeping and watching in her chamber ; still worse and more trying was the necessity of rendering herself agreeable to Mrs Wititterly , who , being in low spirits after the fatigue of the preceding night , of course expected her companion ( else wherefore had she board and salary ?) to be in the best spirits possible .
