# text = But Mr Wititterly's feelings were beyond the power of suppression said Mr Wititterly cried Lord Verisopht said Mr Wititterly In illustration of which remark , Mr Wititterly took a pinch of snuff from his box , and jerked it lightly into the air as an emblem of instability said Mr Wititterly , looking about him with a serious countenance Mr Wititterly told this with a kind of sober exultation , as if it were no trifling distinction for a man to have a wife in such a desperate state , and Mrs Wititterly sighed and looked on , as if she felt the honour , but had determined to bear it as meekly as might be said her husband said Mrs Wititterly , in a faint voice .
