# text = Accordingly Mrs Wititterly broke ground next morning , during a pause in the novel-reading said Mrs Wititterly Here Mrs Wititterly tossed her head -- not passionately , only virtuously -- and remarked , with some appearance of excitement , that she feared that palpitation of the heart was coming on again resumed the lady exclaimed Kate , proudly said Mrs Wititterly , with some violence Kate looked at her , but said nothing resumed Mrs Wititterly said Mrs Wititterly , with a sudden burst of spite Kate looked at her again , but less steadily than before ; and resting her elbow on the table , covered her eyes with her hand said Mrs Wititterly ( this , by the way , must have been some little time before murmured Kate said Mrs Wititterly , with a shrillness of tone quite surprising in so great an invalid she added , waiting with some apparent inconsistency FOR an answer replied Kate said Mrs Wititterly said Mrs Wititterly , closing her chaste eyes as she spoke ; ' it is improper -- quite improper cried Kate , looking upwards and clasping her hands said Mrs Wititterly said Kate with honest indignation cried Kate If poor Kate had possessed the slightest knowledge of the world , she certainly would not have ventured , even in the excitement into which she had been lashed , upon such an injudicious speech as this .
