# text = He made no mention of the way in which he had employed himself ; merely informing Newman that a letter addressed to him under his assumed name at the Post Office , Portsmouth , would readily find him , and entreating that worthy friend to write full particulars of the situation of his mother and sister , and an account of all the grand things that Ralph Nickleby had done for them since his departure from London said Smike , on the night after the letter had been dispatched rejoined Nicholas , with assumed gaiety , for the confession would have made the boy miserable all night inquired Smike replied Nicholas , laughing said Smike , after thinking a little while with his hands folded together , and his eyes bent upon his friend said Nicholas replied Smike , shaking his head cried Nicholas asked Smike replied Nicholas said Smike returned Nicholas asked Smike , bending eagerly forward repeated Smike He had muttered it over to himself some twenty times , when a loud knock at the door disturbed him from his occupation .
