# text = Whether it was the absence of the fetters or not , it made no very deep impression on Mr Lenville's adversary , however , but rather seemed to increase the good-humour expressed in his countenance ; in which stage of the contest , one or two gentlemen , who had come out expressly to witness the pulling of Nicholas's nose , grew impatient , murmuring that if it were to be done at all it had better be done at once , and that if Mr Lenville didn't mean to do it he had better say so , and not keep them waiting there .
