# text = And with the assistance of this lady , and the accomplished Mrs Grudden ( who had quite a genius for making out bills , being a great hand at throwing in the notes of admiration , and knowing from long experience exactly where the largest capitals ought to go ), he seriously applied himself to the composition of the poster sighed Nicholas , as he threw himself back in the prompter's chair , after telegraphing the needful directions to Smike , who had been playing a meagre tailor in the interlude , with one skirt to his coat , and a little pocket-handkerchief with a large hole in it , and a woollen nightcap , and a red nose , and other distinctive marks peculiar to tailors on the stage repeated a female voice behind him , in a kind of plaintive surprise said Nicholas , looking up to see who the speaker was , and recognising Miss Snevellicci said Miss Snevellicci , as the tailor went off on the opposite side , at the end of the piece , with great applause . ( Smike's theatrical name was Digby returned Nicholas rejoined Miss Snevellicci Here Miss Snevellicci stopped , as though waiting to be questioned , but no questioning came , for Nicholas was thinking about more serious matters resumed Miss Snevellicci , after a short silence said Nicholas remarked Miss Snevellicci rejoined Nicholas , shaking his head said Mr Folair , who had come up a little before , and now joined in the conversation asked Nicholas , turning round with some abruptness returned Mr Folair , pulling up the heel of his dancing shoe said Nicholas rejoined the actor , contemplating the effect of his face in a lamp reflector asked Nicholas replied Mr Folair , delighted with the opportunity of saying something disagreeable said Nicholas , contemptuously replied the actor interrupted Nicholas , reddening rejoined the immovable Mr Folair said Nicholas , forcing a smile added Mr Folair cried Nicholas again said Mr Folair , with undisturbed calmness Uttering in a loud voice such of the latter allusions as were complimentary to the unconscious phenomenon , and giving the rest in a confidential ' aside ' to Nicholas , Mr Folair followed the ascent of the curtain with his eyes , regarded with a sneer the reception of Miss Crummles as the Maiden , and , falling back a step or two to advance with the better effect , uttered a preliminary howl , and ' went on ' chattering his teeth and brandishing his tin tomahawk as the Indian Savage thought Nicholas observed Miss Snevellicci in her most winning tones replied Nicholas added Nicholas , as Smike approached returned Miss Snevellicci returned Miss Ledrook , with considerable vivacity Miss Ledrook said no more , but intimated , by a dexterous playfulness , that if Miss Snevellicci couldn't persuade him , nobody could said Miss Snevellicci returned Nicholas rejoined Miss Snevellicci .
