# text = Emporiums of splendid dresses , the materials brought from every quarter of the world ; tempting stores of everything to stimulate and pamper the sated appetite and give new relish to the oft-repeated feast ; vessels of burnished gold and silver , wrought into every exquisite form of vase , and dish , and goblet ; guns , swords , pistols , and patent engines of destruction ; screws and irons for the crooked , clothes for the newly-born , drugs for the sick , coffins for the dead , and churchyards for the buried -- all these jumbled each with the other and flocking side by side , seemed to flit by in motley dance like the fantastic groups of the old Dutch painter , and with the same stern moral for the unheeding restless crowd .
