# text = In however good condition Master Squeers might have been , he certainly did not present this remarkable compactness of person , for on his father's closing his finger and thumb in illustration of his remark , he uttered a sharp cry , and rubbed the place in the most natural manner possible remarked Squeers , a little disconcerted said Squeers , with a triumphant air , as Master Wackford wiped his eyes with the cuff of his jacket returned Ralph , who , for some purposes of his own , seemed desirous to conciliate the schoolmaster replied the proprietor of Dotheboys said Squeers , heaving a sigh , and nodding his head a great many times Mr Squeers indulged in a retrospective look , for some quarter of a minute , as if this allusion to his lady's excellences had naturally led his mind to the peaceful village of Dotheboys near Greta Bridge in Yorkshire ; and then looked at Ralph , as if waiting for him to say something asked Ralph replied Squeers said Squeers , touching first the roots of his hair , and then the toes of his boots asked Mr Squeers , appealing to his son replied Wackford asked Mr Squeers , in a sentimental manner cried Squeers , turning sharp round rejoined his son said Squeers , catching him a smart box on the ear inquired Ralph rejoined Squeers Ralph elevated his eyebrows in a manner which might be expressive of either sympathy or astonishment -- just as the beholder was pleased to take it replied Squeers , who seemed to know the man he had to deal with , too well to suppose that any blinking of the question would induce him to subscribe towards the expenses said Ralph replied Squeers said Ralph rejoined Squeers said Ralph , eyeing the schoolmaster stealthily rejoined Squeers Ralph never laughed , but on this occasion he produced the nearest approach to it that he could , and waiting until Mr Squeers had enjoyed the professional joke to his heart's content , inquired what had brought him to town replied Squeers , scratching his head Ralph looked as if he did not quite understand the observation said Squeers , raising his voice , under the impression that as Ralph failed to comprehend him , he must be deaf added Squeers , moving in his chair with the impatience of an ill-used man observed Ralph replied Squeers asked Ralph replied Squeers said Ralph , who had both spoken and listened mechanically for some time , and seemed to have been thinking rejoined Squeers said Squeers , rattling a bunch of keys in his coat pocket , and muttering something about its being all silver said Ralph , very slowly , and producing , after much rummaging in an old drawer , a penny , a halfpenny , and two farthings said Squeers , bestowing it upon his son added Squeers , closing the door on Master Wackford With this explanation , and a peculiarly knowing look to eke it out , Mr Squeers moved his chair so as to bring himself opposite to Ralph Nickleby at no great distance off ; and having planted it to his entire satisfaction , sat down said Ralph , bending forward a little .
