# text = He was a stout bluff-looking gentleman , with no shirt-collar to speak of , and a beard that had been growing since yesterday morning ; for Dr Lumbey was popular , and the neighbourhood was prolific ; and there had been no less than three other knockers muffled , one after the other within the last forty-eight hours said Dr Lumbey returned Mr Kenwigs said the doctor With this , the doctor laughed ; but he didn't laugh half as much as a married friend of Mrs Kenwigs's , who had just come in from the sick chamber to report progress , and take a small sip of brandy-and - water : and who seemed to consider it one of the best jokes ever launched upon society said Mr Kenwigs , taking his second daughter on his knee said Mr Lumbey , the doctor asked the married lady said Mr Kenwigs said Mr Kenwigs , abruptly , and raising his voice as he spoke said the married lady said Mr Kenwigs , taking a pinch of snuff from the doctor's box , and then sneezing very hard , for he wasn't used to it observed the married lady , nodding her head said Mr Kenwigs , with a portentous look said the married lady , with a glance towards Dr Lumbey pursued Mr Kenwigs Having delivered his sentiments in this form of words , Mr Kenwigs arranged his second daughter's flaxen tail , and bade her be a good girl and mind what her sister , Morleena , said said Mr Lumbey , suddenly stricken with an enthusiastic admiration of Morleena rejoined the married lady Having thus directed the general attention to the young lady in question , the married lady embraced the opportunity of taking another sip of the brandy - and-water -- and a pretty long sip too said Mr Kenwigs , after some reflection Mr Lumbey shook his head with great solemnity , as though to imply that he supposed she must have been rather a dazzler cried Mr Kenwigs said Mr Kenwigs , dropping his voice urged the married lady cried the doctor said the married lady assented Mr Lumbey Mr Kenwigs was about to make some further observations , most probably in confirmation of this opinion , when another married lady , who had looked in to keep up Mrs Kenwigs's spirits , and help to clear off anything in the eating and drinking way that might be going about , put in her head to announce that she had just been down to answer the bell , and that there was a gentleman at the door who wanted to see Mr Kenwigs Shadowy visions of his distinguished relation flitted through the brain of Mr Kenwigs , as this message was delivered ; and under their influence , he dispatched Morleena to show the gentleman up straightway said Mr Kenwigs , standing opposite the door so as to get the earliest glimpse of the visitor , as he came upstairs Nicholas shook hands , kissed his old pupils all round , intrusted a large parcel of toys to the guardianship of Morleena , bowed to the doctor and the married ladies , and inquired after Mrs Kenwigs in a tone of interest , which went to the very heart and soul of the nurse , who had come in to warm some mysterious compound , in a little saucepan over the fire said Nicholas said Mr Kenwigs said Nicholas .
