# text = But , Nicholas and the doctor -- who had been passive at first , doubting very much whether Mr Kenwigs could be in earnest -- interfering to explain the immediate cause of his condition , the indignation of the matrons was changed to pity , and they implored him , with much feeling , to go quietly to bed said Mr Kenwigs , looking around with a plaintive air said one of the married ladies cried a great many voices said Mr Kenwigs , reverting to his calamity cried the matrons generally Mr Kenwigs looked darkly upon the ladies , as if he would prefer its all coming home to HIM , as there was nothing to be got by it ; but he said nothing , and resting his head upon his hand , subsided into a kind of doze .
