# text = Punctual as the counting-house dial , which he maintained to be the best time-keeper in London next after the clock of some old , hidden , unknown church hard by , ( for Tim held the fabled goodness of that at the Horse Guards to be a pleasant fiction , invented by jealous West-enders ,) the old clerk performed the minutest actions of the day , and arranged the minutest articles in the little room , in a precise and regular order , which could not have been exceeded if it had actually been a real glass case , fitted with the choicest curiosities .
