# text = Ralph shrugged his shoulders in deprecation of the intense irritation with which this had been said ; for there was an aggravating , cold distinctness in his speech and manner which so grated on the sick man that he could scarcely endure it asked Sir Mulberry replied Ralph said Ralph , speaking more slowly , and with harsher emphasis interposed Sir Mulberry said Ralph , wilfully mistaking the meaning of the interruption asked Sir Mulberry , clenching his hands and teeth replied Ralph said Ralph , looking eagerly at his questioner said Sir Mulberry observed Ralph , in the same unmoved and quiet manner When Sir Mulberry found coherent words to utter , Ralph bent forward with his hand to his ear , and a face as calm as if its every line of sternness had been cast in iron said the invalid , actually striking at his broken leg in the ecstasy of his passion
