# text = To prepare the mind for such a heavy sleep , its growth must be stopped by rigour and cruelty in childhood ; there must be years of misery and suffering , lightened by no ray of hope ; the chords of the heart , which beat a quick response to the voice of gentleness and affection , must have rusted and broken in their secret places , and bear the lingering echo of no old word of love or kindness .
