# text = Gotten him at thy loodgin replied Squeers , staggering in his chair under the congratulatory blow on the chest which the stout Yorkshireman dealt him repeated John Browdie said Squeers , rubbing his hands inquired John , sitting down close to him Although he could not keep pace with John Browdie's impatience , Mr Squeers related the lucky chance by which Smike had fallen into his hands , as quickly as he could , and , except when he was interrupted by the admiring remarks of his auditors , paused not in the recital until he had brought it to an end observed Squeers , when he had finished , looking very cunning returned the Yorkshireman , shaking him by the hand returned Mr Squeers , who had not expected quite such a ready acceptance of his invitation , or he would have considered twice before he gave it .
