# text = When John Browdie came to be spoken of , he dropped , by slow and gradual degrees , into a chair , and rubbing , his hands upon his knees -- quicker and quicker as the story reached its climax -- burst , at last , into a laugh composed of one loud sonorous having given vent to which , his countenance immediately fell again as he inquired , with the utmost anxiety , whether it was probable that John Browdie and Squeers had come to blows replied Smike Newman scratched his head with a shout of great disappointment , and once more lifting up the mug , applied himself to the contents ; smiling meanwhile , over the rim , with a grim and ghastly smile at Smike said Newman cried Smike returned Newman said Smike cried Newman cried Smike said Newman cried Smike , with increasing eagerness pursued Newman .
