# text = Thou know'd returned his wife replied John returned Nicholas said John said Nicholas replied John said Mrs Browdie ; with an acute perception of the joke though , being a bride herself said John , his eyes twinkling at the idea said his wife said Nicholas , interrupting observed Mrs Browdie , looking very sly said Nicholas , shaking his head said John Browdie , passing his huge forefinger through one of his wife's pretty ringlets , and looking very proud of her said his wife returned John said Nicholas , with the view of stopping some slight connubialities which had begun to pass between Mr and Mrs Browdie , and which rendered the position of a third party in some degree embarrassing , as occasioning him to feel rather in the way than otherwise rejoined Mrs Browdie said Nicholas returned Mrs Browdie said Mrs Browdie , with her archest smile said Nicholas tittered Mrs Browdie cried a shrill female voice With these reproaches Miss Squeers flung the door wide open , and disclosed to the eyes of the astonished Browdies and Nicholas , not only her own symmetrical form , arrayed in the chaste white garments before described ( a little dirtier ), but the form of her brother and father , the pair of Wackfords continued Miss Squeers , who , being excited , aspirated her h's strongly Miss Squeers hesitated a long time for this last epithet , and brought it out triumphantly as last , as if it quite clinched the business suggested Mr Squeers , regarding the spectators with a malevolent eye -- literally A malevolent eye said Miss Squeers remarked Mr Squeers said Miss Squeers , tossing her head , and looking contemptuously at the floor rejoined Mrs Browdie , disregarding all the endeavours of her spouse to restrain her , and forcing herself into a front row demanded Miss Squeers returned Mrs Browdie said Miss Squeers , haughtily interposed John Browdie , nettled by these accumulated attacks on his wife said Miss Squeers , taking him up very quickly said John said Miss Squeers , looking sideways at her parent Here Miss Squeers looked sideways at her father again , who looked sideways at her , as much as to say said Miss Squeers , shaking her curls violently inquired Mrs Browdie , with great suavity of manner retorted Miss Squeers with a low curtsy said the late Miss Price , assuming the matron returned Miss Squeers , sharply Dang it a returned Miss Squeers , with laborious politeness said Miss Squeers , with such a sudden accession of violence that John started in his boots cried Miss Squeers in a solemn voice observed John interposed his wife cried Miss Squeers , bridling up said Mrs Browdie cried Miss Squeers , with another curtsy resumed Mrs Browdie Miss Squeers made no more direct reply than surveying her former friend from top to toe , and elevating her nose in the air with ineffable disdain .
