# text = Add to this , that he was good-looking and intelligent , had a plentiful share of vivacity , was extremely cheerful , and accommodated himself in five minutes' time to all John Browdie's oddities with as much ease as if he had known him from a boy ; and it will be a source of no great wonder that , when they parted for the night , he had produced a most favourable impression , not only upon the worthy Yorkshireman and his wife , but upon Nicholas also , who , revolving all these things in his mind as he made the best of his way home , arrived at the conclusion that he had laid the foundation of a most agreeable and desirable acquaintance thought Nicholas thought Nicholas , coming to the real point in his mind
