# text = So , morning came as usual , and with it business-hours , and with them Mr Frank Cheeryble , and with him a long train of smiles and welcomes from the worthy brothers , and a more grave and clerk-like , but scarcely less hearty reception from Mr Timothy Linkinwater said Tim Linkinwater , getting slowly off his stool , and looking round the counting-house with his back planted against the desk , as was his custom when he had anything very particular to say added Tim , taking off his spectacles , and smiling as with gentle pride said Mr Frank interrupted Tim , with an obstinate air said Tim , folding his arms resolutely said young Cheeryble , laughing said Tim , quite satisfied said Tim , tapping the forefinger of his left hand emphatically with his spectacles
