# text = About six o'clock in the afternoon Mrs Nickleby was thrown into a great flutter of spirits by the long-expected knock at the door , nor was this flutter at all composed by the audible tread of two pair of boots in the passage , which Mrs Nickleby augured , in a breathless state , must be as it certainly was , though not the two Mrs Nickleby expected , because it was Mr Charles Cheeryble , and his nephew , Mr Frank , who made a thousand apologies for his intrusion , which Mrs Nickleby ( having tea-spoons enough and to spare for all ) most graciously received .
