# text = Availing himself of the first opportunity of being alone with Mr Charles Cheeryble at the close of next day , he accordingly related Smike's little history , and modestly but firmly expressed his hope that the good old gentleman would , under such circumstances as he described , hold him justified in adopting the extreme course of interfering between parent and child , and upholding the latter in his disobedience ; even though his horror and dread of his father might seem , and would doubtless be represented as , a thing so repulsive and unnatural , as to render those who countenanced him in it , fit objects of general detestation and abhorrence said Nicholas replied brother Charles Nicholas was delighted to find that the old gentleman spoke so warmly , and in the hope that he might say something more to the same purpose , made no reply said brother Charles After this , brother Charles , who had talked himself into a great heat , stopped to cool a little , and then continued Nicholas coloured , and drew back a step or two said the old gentleman , tapping his desk emphatically said Nicholas returned brother Charles said Nicholas returned brother Charles By this time brother Charles was in such a very warm state of indignation , that Nicholas thought he might venture to put in a word , but the moment he essayed to do so , Mr Cheeryble laid his hand softly upon his arm , and pointed to a chair said the old gentleman , wiping his face After two or three turns across the room he resumed his seat , and drawing his chair nearer to that on which Nicholas was seated , said said Nicholas returned brother Charles cried Nicholas , quite trembling for the moment with his eagerness to hear more said Mr Cheeryble , gravely returned Nicholas said brother Charles ; sadly , as it seemed to his young friend , and with an expression allied to pain replied Nicholas , hurriedly said brother Charles .
