# text = Such was old Arthur Gride , as he sat in a low chair looking up into the face of Ralph Nickleby , who , lounging upon the tall office stool , with his arms upon his knees , looked down into his ; a match for him on whatever errand he had come said Gride , feigning great interest in Ralph's state of health said Ralph , with a peculiar smile , importing that he very well knew it was not on a mere visit of compliment that his friend had come observed Gride replied Ralph , drily .
