# text = In rejoinder to this sally , old Arthur again raised his hands , again chuckled , and again ejaculated which done , he dragged the low chair a little nearer to Ralph's high stool , and looking upwards into his immovable face , said replied Ralph , looking coldly down upon him said old Arthur rejoined Ralph whined Arthur Gride said Ralph cried Arthur , interrupting him , and rubbing his hands in an ecstasy said Ralph , after listening with a curled lip to the old sinner's raptures exclaimed old Arthur retorted Ralph , testily said Arthur Gride , after looking out at the door and carefully reclosing it said Ralph , sharply rejoined old Arthur said Ralph , rendered very irritable by old Arthur's pausing again Whatever reasons there might have been -- and Arthur Gride appeared to have anticipated some -- for the mention of this name producing an effect upon Ralph , or whatever effect it really did produce upon him , he permitted none to manifest itself , but calmly repeated the name several times , as if reflecting when and where he had heard it before said Ralph rejoined Arthur Gride said Ralph , looking vacantly at him said Ralph , shrugging his shoulders said old Arthur rejoined Ralph Naturally as this was said , it was not said so naturally but that a kindred spirit like old Arthur Gride might have discerned a design upon the part of Ralph to lead him on to much more explicit statements and explanations than he would have volunteered , or that Ralph could in all likelihood have obtained by any other means .
