# text = Miss La Creevy earnestly recommended a lady she knew , who would exactly suit Mr Linkinwater , and had a very comfortable property of her own ; but this latter qualification had very little effect upon Tim , who manfully protested that fortune would be no object with him , but that true worth and cheerfulness of disposition were what a man should look for in a wife , and that if he had these , he could find money enough for the moderate wants of both .
