# text = What , then , was the shock which Mrs Nickleby received , when , accosting HER in the most unmistakable manner , he replied in a loud and sonourous voice cried Mrs Nickleby , in a faint tone repeated the old gentleman with which last sound , uttered in a hissing manner between his teeth , the old gentleman swung his arms violently round and round , and at the same time alternately advanced on Mrs Nickleby , and retreated from her , in that species of savage dance with which boys on market-days may be seen to frighten pigs , sheep , and other animals , when they give out obstinate indications of turning down a wrong street .
