# text = Excepting one or two men who , each with a long roll of half-crowns , chequered with a few stray sovereigns , in his left hand , staked their money at every roll of the ball with a business-like sedateness which showed that they were used to it , and had been playing all day , and most probably all the day before , there was no very distinctive character about the players , who were chiefly young men , apparently attracted by curiosity , or staking small sums as part of the amusement of the day , with no very great interest in winning or losing .
