# text = He never took two articles of clothing out together , but always brought them forth , singly , and never failed to shut the wardrobe door , and turn the key , between each visit to its shelves said Arthur Gride , surveying a threadbare coat The result of his cogitations appeared to be unfavourable , for he folded the garment once more , laid it aside , and mounted on a chair to get down another , chirping while he did so : Young , loving , and fair , Oh what happiness there !
