# text = Newman , who in power of taciturnity was excelled by few people , made no attempt to break silence ; and so they went on , until they had very nearly reached Miss Morleena's home , when Mr Lillyvick said returned Newman suggested Newman replied Mr Lillyvick , with another groan ; this time not even disguised by a wheeze interposed Miss Morleena said the collector , with some hesitation returned Miss Morleena , with the energy of both her parents combined Immediately upon the utterance of these words , Mr Lillyvick caught Miss Morleena up in his arms , and kissed her ; and , being by this time at the door of the house where Mr Kenwigs lodged ( which , as has been before mentioned , usually stood wide open ), he walked straight up into Mr Kenwigs's sitting-room , and put Miss Morleena down in the midst .
