# text = Cringing and cowardly to the core by nature , Arthur Gride humbled himself in the dust before Ralph Nickleby , and , even when they had not this stake in common , would have licked his shoes and crawled upon the ground before him rather than venture to return him word for word , or retort upon him in any other spirit than one of the most slavish and abject sycophancy .
