# text = To do Ralph Nickleby justice , he seldom practised this sort of dissimulation ; but he understood those who did , and therefore suffered Bray to say , again and again , with great vehemence , that they were jointly doing a very cruel thing , before he again offered to interpose a word returned Ralph , when the other was at length silent said Bray , biting his nails , and plainly very ill at ease answered Ralph exclaimed Bray , eagerly catching at anything which seemed a justification of himself said Ralph Bray looked at Ralph as if to see whether he spoke in earnest , and having nodded twice or thrice in unqualified assent to what had fallen from him , said said Ralph Ralph followed him , with a steady look , to the door ; and , turning to the bridegroom , when they were again alone , said To this prophecy , so agreeable to his ears , Arthur returned no answer than a cackle of great delight .
