# text = Nay , she even went so far as to hint , obscurely , at an attachment entertained for her daughter by the son of an old neighbour of theirs , one Horatio Peltirogus ( a young gentleman who might have been , at that time , four years old , or thereabouts ), and to represent it , indeed , as almost a settled thing between the families -- only waiting for her daughter's final decision , to come off with the sanction of the church , and to the unspeakable happiness and content of all parties .
