# text = At last , they sat them down in the apartment which Arthur Gride usually inhabited , to rest after their search said Ralph , preparing to depart Gride , who had been peering narrowly about the room , fell , at that moment , upon his knees before a large chest , and uttered a terrible yell said Ralph , looking sternly round screamed Arthur Gride demanded Ralph cried the old man , casting the papers out of the chest , like some beast tearing up the earth said Ralph Still Gride made no answer , but tore and scratched among the papers , and yelled and screeched like a fiend in torment said Ralph , shaking him furiously by the collar cried Ralph , on whom a sudden light appeared to break , for his eyes flashed and his frame trembled with agitation as he clutched Gride by his bony arm shrieked Gride , not heeding the inquiry said Ralph , clutching him still tighter and eyeing him with a sidelong look , so fixed and eager as sufficiently to denote that he had some hidden purpose in what he was about to say screamed the old man , putting his hand on Ralph's mouth cried Ralph shrieked the other , stamping on the ground with the energy of a madman said Ralph rejoined Gride , wringing his hands
