# text = In addition to these influences and persuasions , Ralph drew , with his utmost skill and power , a vivid picture of the defeat which Nicholas would sustain , should they succeed , in linking himself to a beggar , where he expected to wed an heiress -- glanced at the immeasurable importance it must be to a man situated as Squeers , to preserve such a friend as himself -- dwelt on a long train of benefits , conferred since their first acquaintance , when he had reported favourably of his treatment of a sickly boy who had died under his hands ( and whose death was very convenient to Ralph and his clients , but this he did NOT say ), and finally hinted that the fifty pounds might be increased to seventy-five , or , in the event of very great success , even to a hundred .
