# text = He'd have made a good Making a halt in his reflections at this place , Mr Squeers again put his glass to his lips , and drawing a dirty letter from his pocket , proceeded to con over its contents with the air of a man who had read it very often , and now refreshed his memory rather in the absence of better amusement than for any specific information said Mr Squeers Mr Squeers was so much moved by the contemplation of this hardened nature in one so young , that he angrily put up the letter , and sought , in a new train of ideas , a subject of consolation he said Leering with his one eye as if the lady to whom he drank had been actually present , Mr Squeers -- in his enthusiasm , no doubt -- poured out a full glass , and emptied it ; and as the liquor was raw spirits , and he had applied himself to the same bottle more than once already , it is not surprising that he found himself , by this time , in an extremely cheerful state , and quite enough excited for his purpose .
