# text = Newman's arm could no longer be restrained ; the bellows , descending heavily and with unerring aim on the very centre of Mr Squeers's head , felled him to the floor , and stretched him on it flat and senseless Dividing the distance into two days' journey , in order that his charge might sustain the less exhaustion and fatigue from travelling so far , Nicholas , at the end of the second day from their leaving home , found himself within a very few miles of the spot where the happiest years of his life had been passed , and which , while it filled his mind with pleasant and peaceful thoughts , brought back many painful and vivid recollections of the circumstances in which he and his had wandered forth from their old home , cast upon the rough world and the mercy of strangers .
