# text = Satisfied that he was right in his original conjecture , he applied himself to calming the fears of Smike , which , after some time , he partially succeeded in doing , though not in removing the impression upon his mind ; for he still declared , again and again , in the most solemn and fervid manner , that he had positively seen what he had described , and that nothing could ever remove his conviction of its reality .
