# text = That he laboured under some mental or bodily indisposition , and that it was one of no slight kind so to affect a man like him , was sufficiently shown by his haggard face , jaded air , and hollow languid eyes : which he raised at last with a start and a hasty glance around him , as one who suddenly awakes from sleep , and cannot immediately recognise the place in which he finds himself he said He pressed his hand upon his forehead Pushing the table from him while he spoke , as though he loathed the sight of food , he encountered the watch : the hands of which were almost upon noon he said After waiting for another half-hour , he dispatched the woman who kept his house to Newman's lodging , to inquire if he were ill , and why he had not come or sent .
