# text = From that moment , his heart began to fail him he said bitterly cried Newman , standing on tiptoe to look over Tim's head , who had interposed to prevent him reasoned Tim cried Newman , thrusting him aside , and moving his hand as Tim moved , so as to keep him at arm's length Ralph had put a great command upon himself ; but he could not have suppressed a slight start , if he had been certain to be beheaded for it next moment cried Newman With this concluding sentiment , Newman Noggs , who had been perpetually sitting down and getting up again all through his speech , which he had delivered in a series of jerks ; and who was , from the violent exercise and the excitement combined , in a state of most intense and fiery heat ; became , without passing through any intermediate stage , stiff , upright , and motionless , and so remained , staring at Ralph Nickleby with all his might and main .
