# text = When Nicholas began to describe Madeline , he sat with his mouth wide open , nudging Mrs Browdie from time to time , and exclaiming under his breath that she must be and when he heard at last that his young friend had come down purposely to communicate his good fortune , and to convey to him all those assurances of friendship which he could not state with sufficient warmth in writing -- that the only object of his journey was to share his happiness with them , and to tell them that when he was married they must come up to see him , and that Madeline insisted on it as well as he --
